Monolith
A single compile unit where domain dependencies operate within the same process memory space.

Pros: Low Operational complexity, zero network call serialization overhead, simple local transactions.
Cons: Unified blast radius, coupled deployment cycles, hardware scaling bottlenecked by the most resource-intensive module.
Microservices
Decomposes application capabilities into small, independently deployable services organized around specific business domains.

Pros: Independent technology choices, targeted horizontal scaling, isolated fault domains.
Cons: Distributed system complexity, eventual consistency challenges, cross-network debugging overhead, complex deployment requirements.
