Authentication & Authorization
OAuth2 Framework: Standardizes token issuance for delegated access authorization.
OpenID Connect (OIDC): Identity layer built on OAuth2 using JSON Web Tokens (JWT) to securely transport user profile assertions across systems.
Token Verification: API Gateways validate incoming JWT signatures using public key sets (JWKS) supplied by identity providers, isolating signature verification from core microservices.
Ingress Protection
Web Application Firewall (WAF): Evaluates ingress HTTP payloads for common web attack patterns, including SQL injection, cross-site scripting (XSS), and automated bot traffic.
Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS): Enforces browser-level security policies by restricting cross-domain API access via response headers (Access-Control-Allow-Origin, Access-Control-Allow-Methods).


